# TECHNICAL SPECIFICATION: PLUGGABLE AD&D 2E RPG CORE & FULL-SCREEN RULESET EDITOR
**Target Repository:** `https://github.com/Bencepapa/voidcrew` (React, TypeScript, Vite, Zustand, Three.js)
**Module Location:** `src/rpg-core/` (Self-contained, zero-coupling to 3D viewport)
**UI Paradigm:** Full-screen modal overlay (`<StatsEditorModal />`) mirroring the existing Asset Manager pattern, plus headless runtime (`RpgRuntime`) driving live game logic and in-game debug overrides.

---

## 1. ARCHITECTURAL OVERVIEW

The module is split into two strictly decoupled layers inside `src/rpg-core/`:

1. **Headless RPG Runtime (`src/rpg-core/runtime/`):**
   - Pure TypeScript state machine & rules engine (no React, DOM, or Three.js imports).
   - Loads a versioned `RulesetBundle` JSON.
   - Manages live party roster (4 slots, Front/Back row), active monster instances, HP, descending AC, THAC0, Morale, Vancian spellbooks/slots, status effects, and XP progression.
   - Accepts **Action Requests** (`performAttack`, `castSpell`, `rollCheck`, `restParty`, `awardXp`) and returns structured **Outcome Event Payloads** for the 3D engine and HUD to render.
   - Exposes **Live Session Overrides** (`patchActiveMember`, `fullRestoreParty`) so developers can open the editor mid-dungeon, tweak stats/gear/spells, and immediately test combat in 3D.

2. **Full-Screen Ruleset & Stats Editor (`src/rpg-core/editor/`):**
   - Renders as a full-screen modal overlay (`<StatsEditorModal isOpen onClose ... />`) triggered from `EditorBar` next to `Asset Manager`, or standalone in dev mode.
   - Uses `voidcrew` design tokens: Blackened Iron `#17191B` (panel), Raised `#292A28`, Edge `#665B48`, Aged Brass `#C6A365`, Warm Ivory `#EEE3CA`, Muted `#B2ADA0`, HP `#B74541`, Mana `#3C8EB8`.
   - Reuses shared editor primitives (`SharedNumberField` draggable/editable numeric inputs, `HU | EN` i18n toggle, Undo/Redo history stack, Searchable Entity Tree, Right Inspector).
   - Includes a **Rule Validator** and a lightweight **50-Run Batch Auto-Battle & Dice Check Tester** (runs 50 simulated encounters in <10 ms to sanity-check balance, while real spatial combat is tested live inside `voidcrew`).

